        "draftId": "artifact-output-1-linkedin_post",
        "platform": "linkedin_post",
        "text": "Founders shouldn't have to trust AI agents. They should be able to test them.\n\nWe run Harmonia — a team of AI agents for startup content — through an injection screen on 22 labelled texts.\n\nRules alone caught 7 of 12 hidden instructions.\n\nAdd Muse Glimmer, Meta's open-weight model running on a laptop, and it caught all 12 — with none of the 10 clean texts wrongly flagged.\n\nSame approach for reliability: every agent request now goes through a test that checks it against Meta's schema rules. That test caught a missing dependency that would have broken every tool-using agent on launch day.\n\nMy takeaway: don't debate if agents are safe. Publish the test.",
